 "normalization": "The Archive's own OCR of both books reads the Fraktur with many errors and is not used. The leaves named in origin.items were OCR'd in session with the Fraktur model; the OCR of each leaf is kept under original/, and the page images are held by URL and sha256. The OCR is kept as made, with line endings normalized. No text was corrected by hand; the loci keep the OCR's readings and say where those differ from the printed page.",
 "scope": "Two books in part, OCR'd in session from the Fraktur. The Differenzschrift from its Vorerinnerung through the opening sections (leaves n7–n60; the title leaves, which the OCR found blank, are held as images by reference only): the passage on the living spirit of a philosophy, which the historical treatment turns into dead opinion, and the one locating the need of philosophy in division, where the power of union vanishes from life and the oppositions lose their living relation. The lectures on the history of philosophy, volume II, pp. 169–241 (leaves n178–n250): the opening of the period of Plato and Aristotle and the first part of the lecture on Plato, where Hegel cites Tennemann on the exoteric and esoteric, says the most important thing in Plato's philosophy is not grasped at all in Tennemann, a few determinations being gathered as dry ontological ones, and holds that the esoteric is the speculative, written and printed and still hidden from those without the interest to exert themselves. The remainder of both books is in the referenced scans; the rest of the lectures is declared at 32/11.",
 "verified_loci": [
  "Differenz, the Vorerinnerung — 'Vorerinnerung'",
  "Differenz: the living spirit that dwells in a philosophy asks to be born of a kindred spirit — 'Der lebendige Geiſt, der' (the OCR keeps the long s)",
  "Differenz: division is the source of the need of philosophy — 'Quell des Bedürfniſſes der Philoſophie' (the line before reads 'Entzweiung ist der'; the OCR reads Entzweigung)",
  "Differenz: when the power of union vanishes from the life of people and the oppositions lose their living relation — 'Macht der Vereinigung: aus dem: Le-' (the page reads 'die Macht der Vereinigung aus dem Leben der Menschen verschwindet, und die Gegensätze ihre lebendige Beziehung und Wechselwirkung verloren'; the OCR of this leaf is damaged at the gutter)",
  "Lectures, the heading of the period: Plato and Aristotle — 'Erſter Periode dritte Abtheilung: Plato und Ariſtoteles.'",
  "Lectures: exoteric and esoteric philosophy, with Tennemann cited — 'det exoteriſche und eſoteriſche Philoſophie. Tennemann *) ſagt:' (the line begins Man unterschei-; the note cites Tennemann Band II, S. 220)",
  "Lectures: the most important thing in Plato's philosophy is not grasped at all in Tennemann — 'in der platoniſchen Philoſophie iſt bei Tennemann gerade gar nicht aufgefaßt' (the page reads Wichtigste; the OCR reads Widhtigſte)",
  "Lectures: the higher sense of the Philebus and Parmenides, of which Tennemann does not speak — 'Tennemann gar nicht davon die Rede)'",
  "Lectures: the esoteric is the speculative, written and printed, and still hidden — 'Das Eſoteriſche iſt das Spekulative, das geſchrieben und gedru>t iſt' (the page reads gedruckt; the OCR reads gedru>t)"
